[ti:2-05-创业]
[00:00.00]From the information given in the pie chart,
[00:03.32]we can see the survey on the reasons for starting one’s own business among college students in a certain university.
[00:12.04]Those whose ideals are to become entrepreneurs account for 44%,
[00:16.89]the biggest among all the five categories,
[00:20.13]while those who could not find suitable jobs account for 15%.
[00:24.71]As long as they are cautious,
[00:26.87]this kind of real-world experience can greatly benefit their future careers.
[00:32.80]Above all,
[00:33.61]students who launch their own businesses can gain valuable insight into their future career path.
[00:41.07]Some students may even choose to switch majors as a result of insight gained from entrepreneurial activities.
[00:49.43]In addition,
[00:50.41]regardless of whether a student succeeds or fails in a business venture,
[00:55.90]the mere fact of having work experience will come in handy when seeking a full-time job after graduation.
[01:03.81]Employers will regard these students as more ambitious,
[01:08.12]hard-working and mature than graduates who lack such work experience.
[01:13.51]Despite the benefits to students of “getting their feet wet” in the business world,
[01:19.80]it is crucial that they maintain academic studies as a top priority.
